Answer: No, there are no such official records. The search result confirms that while a referral was made, the Department of Justice explicitly declined to prosecute James Comey, stating that "the Department of Justice, however, declined to prosecute Comey."

Source URL: https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/justice-department/justice-department-won-t-prosecute-comey-over-leak-his-memos-n1038326

### Did any U.S. government official publicly announce treason charges against James Comey or John Brennan prior to September 14, 2020?
Answer: No U.S. government official publicly announced formal treason charges against James Comey or John Brennan prior to September 14, 2020. While President Trump accused former FBI officials of treason, the search result makes clear these were rhetorical accusations rather than actual legal proceedings. As the article notes, "Experts have said Mr Trump's treason accusations are baseless," and Trump's remarks—such as listing Comey and others when asked who he was accusing of treason—reflect political rhetoric, not the announcement of criminal charges by any prosecutorial authority.

