## Final Judgement
**Key Insights from Fact-Check:**
The retrieved evidence consistently indicates that, as of September 14, 2020, former FBI Director James Comey and former CIA Director John Brennan had not been charged with any federal crime, let alone multiple counts of treason. The U.S. Department of Justice explicitly declined to prosecute Comey after a referral, and there is no public record or official announcement of any criminal charges, especially for treason, being filed against either individual. While they faced political accusations and were subjects of rhetoric or investigative inquiries, these did not translate into formal legal proceedings or indictments.

**Lacking Information:**
No additional information is required. The evidence is clear and directly addresses all aspects of the claim, showing no basis for the assertion that charges were filed.

**Conclusion:**
Based on the recorded evidence, the claim that former FBI Director James Comey and former CIA Director John Brennan have been charged with multiple counts of treason is not supported. The fact-check found no formal charges, indictments, or public announcements of any such legal actions, with the Department of Justice declining to prosecute Comey and no equivalent records for Brennan. Therefore, the claim is `refuted`.

### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The claim is refuted by multiple authoritative sources confirming that, as of September 2020, neither former FBI Director James Comey nor former CIA Director John Brennan had been charged with any federal crime, including treason. Specifically, the [U.S. Department of Justice declined to prosecute Comey](https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/justice-department/justice-department-won-t-prosecute-comey-over-leak-his-memos-n1038326), and no indictment or official announcement of charges existed for Brennan in public records ([NBC News](https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/justice-department/trump-administration-s-probe-russia-investigation-may-be-nearing-conclusion-n1235904)). While both faced political accusations, these did not result in formal legal proceedings ([The Independent](https://www.the-independent.com/news/world/americas/us-politics/trump-treason-comey-mccabe-strzok-page-white-house-a8928556.html)).